.TH MU2EDAQ\-TAG\-RELEASE 1 "2026-04-21" "Mu2e DAQ" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
mu2edaq\-tag\-release \- create an annotated release tag across mu2edaq\-main and all submodules
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mu2edaq\-tag\-release.sh
.I tag
.RB [ \-m
.IR message ]
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-push ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mu2edaq\-tag\-release.sh
creates an annotated git tag on every submodule of the
.B mu2edaq\-main
meta-repository and then on the parent repository itself.
Tags are pushed to each repository's
.B origin
remote unless
.B \-\-no\-push
is specified.
.PP
If a repository already carries the requested tag it is skipped without error,
making the script safe to re-run after an interrupted release.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I tag
The tag name to create (e.g.\&
.BR v1.2.3 ).
Required.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-m " message"
Annotation message for the tag.
Defaults to
.RI \(lq Release\ <tag> \(rq
when omitted.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Print every action that would be taken without creating or pushing any tags.
Useful for verifying the target repositories and tag name before committing.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-push
Create tags locally in each repository but do not push them to
.BR origin .
After a
.B \-\-no\-push
run the script prints the commands needed to push manually.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
Tag all repositories as
.B v1.0.0
and push immediately:
.EX
    ./mu2edaq\-tag\-release.sh v1.0.0
.EE
Supply a custom annotation message:
.EX
    ./mu2edaq\-tag\-release.sh v1.0.0 \-m "First production release"
.EE
Preview what would happen without making any changes:
.EX
    ./mu2edaq\-tag\-release.sh v1.0.0 \-\-dry\-run
.EE
Create tags locally, then inspect before pushing:
.EX
    ./mu2edaq\-tag\-release.sh v1.0.0 \-\-no\-push
    git submodule foreach 'git push origin v1.0.0'
    git push origin v1.0.0
.EE
.SH BEHAVIOR
.SS Tag ordering
Submodules are tagged first, in the order returned by
.BR "git submodule foreach" .
The parent repository
.RB ( mu2edaq\-main )
is tagged last so its tag always points to a commit that references already-tagged submodule states.
.SS Skipping existing tags
If the requested tag already exists in a repository that repository is skipped
and a
.B SKIP
message is printed.
This allows a failed run to be retried without manually deleting partial tags.
.SS Annotated tags
All tags created by this script are annotated (
.B git tag \-a
), which records the tagger identity, date, and message in the git object
database.
Lightweight tags are not used.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All tags were created (and pushed, unless
.B \-\-no\-push
was given) successfully.
.TP
.B non-zero
A git operation failed.
The script exits immediately on the first error due to
.BR "set \-euo pipefail" .
.SH FILES
.TP
.B .gitmodules
Defines the submodule paths and remote URLs used by this script.
Located at the root of the
.B mu2edaq\-main
repository.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2edaq\-bootstrap (1),
.BR git (1),
.BR git\-tag (1),
.BR git\-submodule (1)
.SH REPOSITORY
.UR https://github.com/Mu2e/mu2edaq-main
https://github.com/Mu2e/mu2edaq-main
.UE
